**SECURED — `e4-long-road` on `e4-long-road-01`, trail. First secure.**

`w12 / 360.000s / 0g / 34 calls / 342 kills · fnv1a32:b32a1b56` — tape: `artifacts/heat11/opus/e4-long-road/attempt-1-tape.json`. 4 runs, 1 scored attempt, `worldModel: sim-import`. Tune 2 secured on its first ride; attempt 1 re-rode it byte-identical (34 entries, tapes differ only in the random `id`).

**What decided it, in two numbers.** The run holds 36 fuel total and the Hauler burns 3/second: 370 wu of ungraded road costs 123 fuel, and graded (2.5× speed, 0.4× burn) it costs 19.7. So the single free `GRADE` at the road's west stake, 8 wu from where the hero starts, is the whole contract. Measured 21.557 drawn, 14.443 left.

The convoy latch is an exact-position one — `MotorSocket.ts:345` needs `leaderDistance ≥ 370 − 1e-6`, i.e. the Hauler at rest *on* (190,0). That's reachable because the Prospector snaps onto its MOVE_TO target (`Embodiment.ts:272`) and `HOLD` re-issues movement every tick, so a held worker never drifts. When a fuel-limited final step left the Hauler 0.093 short, a second `HAUL` closed it for 0.005 fuel.

**The wall was never the errand — it was the hero.** Tune 1 solved the convoy at t=120 and still died at t=164 with gold 0 and zero works, because no build zone comes within 32 wu of the hero's stake against a 16 wu turret range. The fix was geometric: enemies converge from the gates at (0,±46) onto (−180,0), so the west way-station's north edge covers both the south stream (z ≈ −11, inside the box) and the graded road they prefer at z = 0. That reordering — fort first, errand at wave 5 — is the entire difference between the two runs.

Two findings for the county:
- **The 2026-09-02 RESKIN measurement is out of date on this build.** The secure is `wave ≥ 12` **AND** `now.motor.objective.arrived`, the road lever is decisive rather than optional, and of the four Motor maps I've ridden this is the one where E4 mattered most.
- **The map's headline fiction isn't what the engine runs.** Its own manifest declares `convoy-claim-consumer: "missing"` — no moving claim, no lead-Hauler loss; the loss is `hero_down` on a static stake. The authored `restStops` (45s anchorage) appear in no view field and have no verb, and `convoy.members[].gap` is published but inert.

Margin was wide: hero never below 92 of its running max, finished 127/175 at level 16, all four works standing and never wrecked, three waves of slack on the errand. The thin thing was the purse — 180 gold panned all run, which bought the fort exactly and nothing more.

Report and outcome file are on disk with the four verbatim sections. No tracked file was modified. One note: `attempt-1-tape.json`, `tune-1/2/3-tape.json` appeared untracked at the repo root during the session — not mine (all my `--tape` paths were inside my workspace, confirmed by the directory listing), most likely the concurrent rig's; I left them alone.
